From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 05:04:07 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: share one test harness across the driver tests

Every KosmicKrisp test carried its own copy of the same checks.  30 C and
Objective-C tests defined CHECK in three shapes (two boolean messages and a
VkResult form), twelve of them the same LOAD_I and LOAD_D, 27 C++ tests and
benchmarks the same require() and load<>(), and the line-planner helper its
own KK_TEST_CHECK.  tests/kk_test.h now holds one boolean CHECK, one VK_CHECK
and the C and C++ loaders; the VkResult-form tests and the one CHECK_VK use
VK_CHECK.  Every check still names its expression and aborts in every build,
and the C++ require() still exits with status 1.

The Meson stanzas of the four uniform families - Vulkan-level C++ tests,
whole-library internal tests, header-only helper tests and NIR-to-MSL
compiler tests - become loops over their names and timeouts.  The
dynamically uniform TES sampler test, a near-copy of the uniform one, becomes
an argument of it, and the point-clip test reads the polygon-point fragment
shader it had duplicated byte for byte.  Test names and timeouts are
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
